 {"id": "LORE-020", "title": "[P2] absorb --window: undocumented trail contract + --source silently dropped from sweep proposals", "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "phase": "cli", "repo": "https://github.com/get-h3/lore", "detail": "Two defects, one user-facing flow (dogfood 2026-09-25). (a) The sweep consumes a logsey-EXPORT payload only (lore/evidence.py parse_logsey_export: a line matching 'logsey export', a fenced block, evidence lines starting with a BARE ISO timestamp). A natural incident trail with bracketed '[2026-09-25 06:12]' prefixes returns 'no classifiable evidence blocks in the trail' exit 0 with NO hint about the expected shape — the user has to read source. (b) `lore absorb --window 2h ... --source dogfood-dagger` accepts --source but the sweep payload never records it: absorb_sweep() (lore/absorb.py:182) has no source parameter (the CLI wiring at lore/__main__.py:236 passes source only on the --class path; absorb_proposal keeps it). The LORE-009 contract says the provenance marker is recorded in the payload — sweep proposals currently lose it. Fix direction: document the export shape in --help/README, emit a 'input did not claim to be a logsey export — expected: logsey export header + fenced block + ISO-timestamped lines' hint on the empty result, and thread source through absorb_sweep into each proposal (plus tests).", "reasoning": "Dogfood 2026-09-25 real scribe flow — two trail attempts, source drop proven by grep of sweep output vs single-class absorb output", "source": "dogfood-lore-2026-09-25", "ts": "2026-09-25T08:12:29+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-09-25T09:12:00+00:00", "worker_status": "complete", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/lore-LORE-020", "branch": "wt/LORE-020", "foreman_note": "Tier-2 verdict 65110f24 PASS/COMPLETE (dir 88d17a5b). Merged-tree gate: 262 passed, ruff clean. Foreman guard --full PASS whole-tree on final tree (guard-20260925T085853.224792Z.log).", "commit_hash": "cdb8499", "worker_summary": "Wave-7 worker (worktree wt/LORE-020): absorb --window now plumbs args.source into absorb_sweep per-class proposals (omit = payload keeps original shape, matching the single-proposal contract); trail contract documented in docs/INSTALL.md (stdin or --trail-file, logsey export format, empty-trail exit 0, propose-not-write); tests/test_lore020_absorb_window.py regression tests RED-proven. Live proof: 'echo <trail> | lore absorb --window 2h --source dogfood-dagger' carries source in every proposal. Merged 188cf1a.", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "lines_added": "114", "lines_removed": "8", "completed_at": "2026-09-25 09:12:00"}
 {"id": "LORE-021", "title": "[P3] Library naming: NearMiss.raw_score vs CLI's printed 'score='; Classification.evidence is dicts, not objects", "status": "complete", "priority": "P3", "phase": "api", "repo": "https://github.com/get-h3/lore", "detail": "External consumer friction (dogfood 2026-09-25, script outside the repo, public API only): (a) near_misses() returns NearMiss with field raw_score (lore/classifier.py:49) while the CLI prints 'score=0.33' — a consumer reading CLI output first writes .score and gets AttributeError; (b) Classification.evidence is a list of DICTS (e[\"kind\"], e[\"detail\"]), while the same object carries typed fields elsewhere and the old usage skill implied object access. Fix direction: add a `score` alias property on NearMiss (or rename the CLI print to raw_score=) and document/normalize the evidence element shape in the public API docs. Workaround documented in skills/lore-usage/SKILL.md.", "reasoning": "Dogfood 2026-09-25 library-consumer probe — 2 AttributeErrors before the consumer ran clean", "source": "dogfood-lore-2026-09-25", "ts": "2026-09-25T08:12:29+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-09-25T09:12:00+00:00", "worker_status": "complete", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/lore-LORE-021", "branch": "wt/LORE-021", "foreman_note": "Tier-2 verdict 11136f9b PASS/COMPLETE (dir 05b108aa). Merged-tree gate: 269 passed, ruff clean. Foreman guard --full PASS whole-tree on final tree (guard-20260925T085853.224792Z.log).", "commit_hash": "718b9e6", "worker_summary": "Wave-7 worker (worktree wt/LORE-021): lore/classifier.py docstrings pinned — NearMiss.raw_score (raw keyword fraction) vs CLI-printed band-scaled 'score=', Classification.evidence = list of plain dicts with keys kind/detail. tests/test_lore021_naming_docs.py pins both contracts mechanically (uses the module's own scaling, no duplicated math). Zero behavior change (docstrings only). Merged c7a7c2c.", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "lines_added": "136", "lines_removed":