 {"id":"QA-LORE-1","status":"complete","title":"[P3] QA: no release tags in repo — upgrade-path cell untestable (QA foreman live finding)","priority":"P3","phase":"qa","repo":"https://github.com/get-h3/lore","detail":"QA foreman fresh-system battery on bunker-las-02 (agent 292f6c76, 2026-09-23) ran the upgrade cell and got N/A: `git tag -l` on a fresh clone is empty, so there is no released version to install-over and the upgrade path is untested. Today this is cheap (v0.1.0 unreleased, package installs clean via uv/pip). The cost arrives with the first real release: if v0.1.x and v0.2.0 drift in config/state layout, nobody has proven an in-place upgrade works. Fix direction: tag v0.1.0 at the first releasable milestone so the next QA cycle can run a real install-old-then-upgrade cell.","reasoning":"Foreman-direct execution in tick lore-2026-09-25-10-28-50. Fix direction already satisfied: v0.1.0 tagged 2026-09-24 (c655666) and pushed. Executed the actual upgrade-path cell in a fresh venv: pip install git+https://github.com/get-h3/lore@v0.1.0 -> v0.1.0, lore CLI works (match smoke). pip install --upgrade @main was a SILENT NO-OP (same version string 0.1.0, pip skips reinstall) — real cell finding. Fix: bumped version to 0.1.1 + CHANGELOG entry (commit 02286e4, pushed). Re-ran cell on pushed main: v0.1.0 -> upgrade -> 0.1.1, installed classifier hash cad69dfc == repo main hash (code swap proven), match smoke green, 269/269 tests pass on the upgraded install.","commit_hash":"02286e4","branch":"main","worker_status":"foreman-direct","worker_summary":"Upgrade-path cell proven end-to-end in fresh venvs: fresh install v0.1.0 from public GitHub succeeds and CLI works; upgrade to main now reinstalls (0.1.0->0.1.1) and lands main code (hash-verified); 269 tests pass post-upgrade. Found+fixed: same-version no-op upgrade (version bump 02286e4).","foreman_note":"Tagging existed since 09-24; the residual work was executing the cell + the no-op-upgrade fix. Judge: Tier-2 PASS COMPLETE (async job-7aba9ff7, verdict dir .gitreins/history/2026-09-25/a7eedbf3, commit 02286e4).","guard_result":"Tier-1 PASS 82f6a6bf; Tier-2 PASS COMPLETE (async)","completed_at":"2026-09-25T10:34:08+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-25T10:34:08+00:00","ts":"2026-09-25T10:34:08+00:00"}
-{"id": "LORE-022", "status": "open", "priority": "P1", "phase": "docs", "title": "[P1] Freshness promise contradiction: docs say last_validated is populated by validate --execute, but apply_lint never stamps it — every runbook stays 'no data' forever", "detail": "Dogfood 2026-09-25 run 3 (the re-validation/anti-rot surface, untouched by prior runs). README.md:281 and audit's own summary line ('last_validated is populated only by `lore validate --execute` runs') promise the lint stamps freshness. Measured: a full `lore validate --execute` sweep (outcomes 5 ok / 23 error / 1 refused) AND a fully-green single-class run (`lore validate --class shared-checkout-collision --execute` -> 3/3 ok) both leave `lore show` at 'Last validated: no data (never validated)' and `lore audit` at 'no data'. Source confirms this is intent, not a bug: lore/validate.py docstring — apply_lint NEVER sets last_validated or status='validated'; operator attestation only (propose-not-write). The implementation is defensible; the promise is wrong in two user-visible places. Effect: the auditor persona (PRD US-3) can never see a validated runbook on v0.1.x — 'does it still work?' is answerable only by reading lint output, not by the freshness field the docs point at. Fix direction: (a) docs truth sweep — README/audit-summary state 'never populated in v0.1; operator attestation planned; the lint's stale flag is the freshness signal'; or (b) ship the planned operator-attestation step (explicit command stamping last_validated after a human reviews an --execute run). Do NOT stamp from apply_lint — that would fabricate the honesty law.", "reasoning": "Run-3 dogfood: two --execute runs (full sweep + green single-class) on HEAD 3ab56f5; contradiction proven by grep of README:281 vs show/audit output; intent verified in lore/validate.py docstring.", "repo": "https://github.com/get-h3/lore", "source": "dogfood-lore-2026-09-25-run3", "ts": "2026-09-25T16:16:59+00:00"}
